iew": "Pennsylvania remains the quintessential presidential battleground, and the 2028 open race starts essentially even. The state's partisan lean favors Republicans by about a point, and with a term-limited incumbent leaving the ballot, neither side enjoys incumbency advantages. No presidential polls or expert ratings are yet available, keeping uncertainty high.\n\nDown-ballot signals cut both ways: Governor Shapiro is polling far ahead in his reelection race, suggesting Democratic organizational strength, while voters remain divided on his national ambitions. Until direct presidential polling arrives, the race is best treated as a genuine tossup with a slight Republican edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4565, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5269, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.504, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.475, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4803, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5405, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.485, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4847, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4588, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4605, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.5147, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4565, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.4822, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.4835, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.4545, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.4594, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.5591, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.5359, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.4587, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.5531, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.5619, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.5599, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.5615, "margin": 1.5}, 